Goal: modify detection to also treat other IPython shells as Jupyter. Perhaps checking for attribute `parent`? Look at docs. In Databricks, the IPython class name might be "InteractiveShell". We could also check for presence of "IPKernelApp" or environment variable "DATABRICKS_RUNTIME_VERSION"? Simpler: treat any IPython shell not TerminalInteractiveShell as Jupyter.

Current logic:

if "google.colab" in str(ipython.__class__) or shell == "ZMQInteractiveShell":
    return True
elif shell == "TerminalInteractiveShell":
    return False
else:
    return False

